    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The maintenance schedule can vary, but generally, a sealed stone floor may need resealing every 3-5 years, whereas maintenance steps like cleaning could be needed monthly or during every full cleaning. Regular use of a soft-bristle broom or vacuum, followed by a pH-neutral cleaner, will keep the stone clean and prevent scuff marks.\n\nSome types of natural stone, like honed granite, are better at hiding scratches compared to raw or honed marble. Honed finishes, in general, are less prone to get dirty and are less likely to pick up scuff marks compared to other finishes, though no natural stone is immune to surface marks. Both the polishing method and the type of sealant used when sealing are factors contributing to scratch resistance.",
